According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [4adba2f4da302fee]. In the input fence[ A S ], the code fence contains JSON object A and sentence S. Since the fence holds an object, A is the scored object. In the rewritten text fence[ S ], the JSON object A is removed from inside the code fence, leaving only the sentence S. The fence no longer holds an object, and there are no top-level objects outside the fence. Thus the recovered object moves from {"a": 1} to NO_OBJECT.